# Superseded release archives.
#
# 112 historical build artifacts, ~23 MB. Excluded because they are derived: given a
# base release ZIP, tools/build_release.py reproduces a release byte-for-byte
# (verified for v0.4.1: sha256 4fd51ef648a4e2ce4cb705edebcd4ddc4fc52cfb11e60c5be172d6a5fe64f9a3).
#
# The CURRENT release ZIP at the repo root is deliberately NOT ignored. It is a build
# INPUT, not just an artifact: addon/config.bin is pre-binarized and the base PBO
# defines the entry set that pack_pbo fills from addon/, so without it the project
# cannot be built at all.
releases/

# Local session memory from the remember plugin. Not project content.
.remember/

# Build scratch
# build_release.py --out-dir build/check writes a throwaway release here when
# proving that a rebuild still reproduces a shipped PBO byte for byte.
build/
*.pbo
!addon/**/*.pbo
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp

# Signing keys. The real ones live OUTSIDE this repository (see build_release.py step 3);
# this is a backstop so a key copied in by accident can never be committed. A private key
# in a public history lets anyone sign a hostile PBO that passes as TLB CARP.
*.biprivatekey
*.bikey

# Per-contributor editor and assistant instruction files. The rules themselves live in
# CONTRIBUTING.md, which is the one copy and is written for whoever is reading. Anything
# that points a particular tool at it is personal setup, not project content.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/
.cursorrules
.github/copilot-instructions.md
